# Equinox Testing Rules

## Critical Business Tests

Always test:

### Sales Order → Invoice

* one SO can create multiple invoices
* invoice cannot exceed remaining SO quantity
* fully invoiced SO cannot create additional quantity
* partial invoicing works correctly

### Invoice → ATW/DR

* one Invoice can create multiple ATW/DR documents
* ATW/DR cannot exceed remaining invoice quantity
* fully allocated invoice cannot allocate additional quantity
* partial allocation works correctly

### ATW/DR → Withdrawal Slip

* one ATW/DR can create one WS
* second WS creation is rejected
* WS quantity cannot exceed ATW/DR quantity

### Authorization

Test every role:

* ADMIN
* SALES
* WAREHOUSE
* ACCOUNTING

Verify permissions server-side, not only through UI.

### Cancellation

Verify:

* cancelled documents cannot be used incorrectly
* cancellation reason is recorded
* cancelled transactions remain in history

## Regression

After changing business logic, run all related tests.

## Before Completion

Run:

* lint
* typecheck
* unit tests
* integration tests where applicable
* production build

Do not claim a feature is complete if the production build fails.
